{"name":"Beau Monde","hex":"#7db39e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"beau monde","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The fashionable part of society."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beau_monde"}],"entries":[{"title":"Beau Monde","blocks":[{"text":"Beau Monde is a Dutch language monthly glamour and lifestyle magazine published in Amsterdam, Netherlands. The phrase \"Beau monde\", also used in English, means fashionable society. Beau Monde is published out of the Pijper Media offices in Amsterdam and Groningen. It targets women between 21 and 45 years of age. The magazine organizes an annual \"Beau Monde Award\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beau_Monde","wikidata":"Q12721607"},{"title":"High society","blocks":[{"text":"High society, sometimes simply Society, is the behavior and lifestyle of people with the highest levels of wealth, power, fame and social status. It includes their related affiliations, social events and practices. Upscale social clubs were open to men based on assessments of their ranking and role within high society. In American high society, the Social Register was traditionally a key resource for identifying qualified members. For a global perspective, see upper class. The quality of housing, clothing, servants and dining were visible marks of membership."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Caroline_Astor_and_her_guest%2C_New_York_1902.jpg/330px-Caroline_Astor_and_her_guest%2C_New_York_1902.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/High_society","wikidata":"Q2910239"},{"title":"Monde","blocks":[{"text":"A monde, meaning 'world' in French, is an orb located near the top of a crown. It represents, as the name suggests, the world that the monarch rules. It is the point at which a crown's half arches meet. It is usually topped off either with a national or religious symbol, for example a cross in Christian countries."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monde","wikidata":"Q6898686"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/James_Tissot_-_Too_Early.jpg/500px-James_Tissot_-_Too_Early.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/James_Tissot_-_Too_Early.jpg/500px-James_Tissot_-_Too_Early.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Too Early by James Tissot, 1873","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJames_Tissot_-_Too_Early.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Mrs_William_Astor_%28Caroline_Webster_Schermerhorn%29%2C_by_Carolus-Duran.jpg/500px-Mrs_William_Astor_%28Caroline_Webster_Schermerhorn%29%2C_by_Carolus-Duran.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Mrs_William_Astor_%28Caroline_Webster_Schermerhorn%29%2C_by_Carolus-Duran.jpg/1280px-Mrs_William_Astor_%28Caroline_Webster_Schermerhorn%29%2C_by_Carolus-Duran.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Mrs_William_Astor_%28Caroline_Webster_Schermerhorn%29%2C_by_Carolus-Duran.jpg/500px-Mrs_William_Astor_%28Caroline_Webster_Schermerhorn%29%2C_by_Carolus-Duran.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mrs. William Astor painted by Carolus-Duran in 1890, presented at the 1894 Great Portrait Exhibition","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMrs_William_Astor_(Caroline_Webster_Schermerhorn)%2C_by_Carolus-Duran.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Sargent_Portrait_of_Lady_Helen_Vincent_1904.jpg/500px-Sargent_Portrait_of_Lady_Helen_Vincent_1904.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, 